---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

// /metadax/guide/play-and-print/ -- open a package in the player, and print the
// learner page and the guide key. Every claim here matches the player
// (/metadax/play/) and the print page (/metadax/play/print): nothing saved or
// sent; "Print this" renders the learner side; the guide key is a separate page;
// the spoken-sound item; companion notes are guide-only and never printed.
---
<Base title="Open and print a Meta DAX package" description="Open your lesson package in the player, read your page and your child's, then print the learner page and the guide key. Everything runs in your browser; nothing is saved or sent." wide>
  <section class="lede">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/metadax/">Meta DAX</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/metadax/guide/">Help</a> &rsaquo; Open &amp; print</p>
    <h1>Open it and print it</h1>
    <p class="lede-text">
      Once you have a package &mdash; the <code>metadax-package</code> JSON from the
      skill or an AI chat &mdash; the player opens it. One shared player renders
      every package. Everything runs in your browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-open">
    <h2 id="h-open">Open it in the player</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Go to the player: <a href="/metadax/play/">daxfoundation.org/metadax/play/</a>.</li>
      <li>Paste your package JSON into &ldquo;Open your package&rdquo; and press <strong>Play</strong>.</li>
      <li>You get two tabs: <strong>For you</strong> (the guide) and <strong>For the learner</strong> (your child&rsquo;s side, with the game). Read your page first.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="body">
      The player says it plainly: <em>&ldquo;Nothing here is saved or sent
      anywhere.&rdquo;</em> It works offline once the page has loaded &mdash; you can
      save the player page and drop the JSON into it for a fully offline file.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-print">
    <h2 id="h-print">Print the learner page and the guide key</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Press <strong>Print this</strong>. The printed version is paper-first and in
      black and white, and it prints two things in order:
    </p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li><strong>The learner page</strong> &mdash; the part your child works from. The games become questions with a box to tick and a line to write on. No answers are shown here.</li>
      <li><strong>The guide key</strong> &mdash; on its own page at the end. It carries the answer to each question and one line of why. As it says: <em>&ldquo;Keep this page; the learner page above has none of it.&rdquo;</em></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="body">
      So you can hand your child their pages and keep the guide key yourself. Every
      sheet carries the same two lines at the foot: <em>behaviour never
      diagnoses</em>, and <em>a way, never the way</em>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-spoken">
    <h2 id="h-spoken">The &ldquo;say it, then find it&rdquo; item</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Some lessons &mdash; early reading especially &mdash; include a spoken-sound
      item. <strong>You say the prompt aloud; your child taps or circles the one
      they hear.</strong> The page itself speaks nothing. On screen the answer is
      marked as a preview for you; in print the answer stays off the learner page
      and sits only in the guide key.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-companion">
    <h2 id="h-companion">Companion notes (for the guide only)</h2>
    <p class="body">
      A package can come with optional <strong>companion notes</strong> &mdash; a
      small sidecar file. If you have one, open &ldquo;Companion notes&rdquo; in the
      player and paste it in. Only its guide-facing notes are shown, and only on
      your &ldquo;For you&rdquo; tab &mdash; never on your child&rsquo;s side, and
      never in print. If the notes don&rsquo;t match the expected shape, the player
      simply plays the package without them.
    </p>
    <p class="out">
      <a href="/metadax/guide/next-session/">Next: session two, and several kids &rarr;</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/metadax/guide/">Back to the guide</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { padding-block: 3rem 2rem; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .eyebrow a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .eyebrow a:hover, .eyebrow a:focus-visible { color: var(--fg); }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.2rem + 2.6vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.22; letter-spacing: -0.012em; max-width: 20em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .lede-text { margin: 0; max-width: 40em; color: #cfcfcf; }

  .block { padding-block: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  strong { font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg); }
  .body { margin: 0; max-width: 40em; color: #cfcfcf; }
  .body + .body, .body + .out, .out + .body, .body + .plain, .plain + .body, .steps + .body { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .body a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  .body a:hover, .body a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }
  .steps, .plain { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; max-width: 42em; color: #cfcfcf; }
  .steps li + li, .plain li + li { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 8%, transparent); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; }

  .out { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .out span { color: var(--faint); margin-inline: 0.5rem; }
  .out a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  .out a:hover, .out a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }
</style>
